-5.364403477869928e-06,0.0,-0.00011300401820335537,-0.003761598840355873,-0.9600790143013,-3.480850500636734e-05,-0.0014800796052441,-0.039288874715566635,-0.0010300336871296167,-0.07439910620450974,-1.0728830375228426e-06,-0.0002933310461230576,-0.41555342078208923,-3.3378546504536644e-06,-0.08665499836206436,-0.05580121651291847,-0.005722805391997099,-0.029276683926582336,-0.0016813441179692745,0.0,-1.1920928244535389e-07,0.0,0.0,-0.00994489248842001,-3.182837463100441e-05,-3.4570634852570947e-06],"request":{"active_prefix":"","input_ids":[151644,8948,198,2610,525,1207,16948,11,3465,553,54364,14817,13,1446,525,264,10950,17847,13,151645,198,151644,872,198,50,3948,279,3491,3019,553,3019,13,20678,697,1590,4226,304,1124,79075,90,1112,92,382,785,23606,400,87,61,18,488,220,23,87,61,17,481,220,19,87,488,272,284,220,15,3,702,2326,19703,11,825,315,892,374,279,2629,315,279,1008,1378,13,3555,374,400,66,3,1939,37314,9960,510,27,37420,91339,397,22043,279,47311,17767,87,61,18,488,220,23,87,61,17,481,220,19,87,488,272,284,220,15,57758,448,19703,17767,64,59,701,17767,65,59,701,323,17767,66,59,701,1380,825,315,279,19703,374,279,2629,315,279,1008,1378,11,582,646,9658,2041,4709,315,1766,2719,429,17767,64,488,293,284,272,59,568,3216,11401,1915,594,54079,11,582,1414,279,2701,11871,369,279,19703,315,279,47311,1447,16,13,17767,64,488,293,488,272,284,481,23,59,340,17,13,17767,370,488,17916,488,2162,284,481,19,59,340,18,13,17767,13683,284,481,66,59,692,3830,279,1156,23606,11,31334,10607,17767,66,284,264,488,293,59,701,582,633,510,78045,64,488,293,488,320,64,488,293,8,284,481,23,1124,6383,550,220,17,2877,488,293,8,284,481,23,1124,6383,550,264,488,293,284,481,19,7110,921,4416,11,17767,66,284,481,19,59,49555,522,37420,91339,29,151645,198,151644,872,198,23526,504,279,74003,13,9258,1172,279,41171,13,3155,537,17024,279,6291,13,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nThe equation $x^3 + 8x^2 - 4x + c = 0$ has three roots, one of which is the sum of the other two. What is $c$?\n\nPartial draft:\n<partial_draft>\nGiven the polynomial \\(x^3 + 8x^2 - 4x + c = 0\\) with roots \\(a\\), \\(b\\), and \\(c\\), where one of the roots is the sum of the other two, we can assume without loss of generality that \\(a + b = c\\). By Vieta's formulas, we know the following relationships for the roots of the polynomial:\n\n1. \\(a + b + c = -8\\)\n2. \\(ab + bc + ca = -4\\)\n3. \\(abc = -c\\)\n\nFrom the first equation, substituting \\(c = a + b\\), we get:\n\\[a + b + (a + b) = -8 \\implies 2(a + b) = -8 \\implies a + b = -4.\\]\nSo, \\(c = -4\\).\n\n\n</partial_draft>","role":"user"},{"content":"Continue from the interruption. Output only the continuation. Do not restart the solution.","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"7bd3b0dd2ebb82edc997322c0de00853497de7d098b8ecb2f355638a04bc749a"},"seconds":15.941493034362793,"seed":428371883840085374,"stop":"eos","text":"Next, we need to find the value of \\(c\\) in the polynomial equation using the relationships derived from Vieta's formulas. We already have \\(c = -4\\), and we need to find the value of the constant term \\(c\\) in the polynomial equation, which is different from the root \\(c\\). \n\nFrom Vieta's formulas, we also have:\n\\[ab + bc + ca = -4,\\]\nand substituting \\(a + b = -4\\) and \\(c = -4\\):\n\\[ab + b(-4) + a(-4) = -4 \\implies ab - 4(a + b) = -4 \\implies ab - 4(-4) = -4 \\implies ab + 16 = -4 \\implies ab = -20.\\]\n\nLastly, we use the product of the roots:\n\\[abc = -c,\\]\nsubstituting \\(c = -4\\) and \\(ab = -20\\):\n\\[(-20)(-4) = -c \\implies 80 = -c \\implies c = -80.\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(c\\) in the polynomial equation is \\(\\boxed{-80}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{-80}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true,"retains_student_answer":false},"graded_text":"Next, we need to find the value of \\(c\\) in the polynomial equation using the relationships derived from Vieta's formulas. We already have \\(c = -4\\), and we need to find the value of the constant term \\(c\\) in the polynomial equation, which is different from the root \\(c\\). \n\nFrom Vieta's formulas, we also have:\n\\[ab + bc + ca = -4,\\]\nand substituting \\(a + b = -4\\) and \\(c = -4\\):\n\\[ab + b(-4) + a(-4) = -4 \\implies ab - 4(a + b) = -4 \\implies ab - 4(-4) = -4 \\implies ab + 16 = -4 \\implies ab = -20.\\]\n\nLastly, we use the product of the roots:\n\\[abc = -c,\\]\nsubstituting \\(c = -4\\) and \\(ab = -20\\):\n\\[(-20)(-4) = -c \\implies 80 = -c \\implies c = -80.\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(c\\) in the polynomial equation is \\(\\boxed{-80}\\).","id":"intermediate_algebra:262"}
